      "writtenOn": "2021-09-27T14:33:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding is that this flags all \"drivers\" that include xperms, which is later read out by avc_has_extended_perms to figure out whether it needs to compute an xperms decision. Given that all netlink xperms are included in driver 0, the presence of those xperms means that driver 0 should be flagged.\n\nAlternatively, I could rewrite this to correspond to the AVTAB_XPERMS_IOCTLFUNCTION case above, where it would read the driver (which will always be 0) from the node-\u003edatum.u.xperms-\u003edriver field. Let me know what you prefer.",
      "parentUuid": "539ea483_d9049805",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 612,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 612,
        "endChar": 27
      },
